From 5fe1bf502a31e79891fabeb20b2549eb8bbe954e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Martin=20Storsj=C3=B6?= <martin@martin.st>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 12:12:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] compat: Fix building with newer versions of MSVC

Previously, MSVC's preprocessor happily parsed the #if line that
references __has_include_next, and ignored it (and as the start of
the line, `defined(__clang__)`, evaluates to zero, it doesn't make any
difference anyway).

Since MSVC around version 19.52.36629 (19.52 is currently in preview,
not a stable release), MSVC now errors out on this expression:

    ../include/compat/msvc\stdatomic.h(35): error C7780: function-like macro '__has_include_next' is not defined
    ../include/compat/msvc\stdatomic.h(35): fatal error C1017: invalid integer constant expression

Add a fallback definition of __has_include_next, to let the MSVC
preprocessor handle this cleanly.

In practice, this header isn't ever used with Clang though - if
stdatomic.h exists, then we don't add include/compat/msvc at all,
and we only add this directory if actually compiling with MSVC.

(cherry-picked from commit a34e0685b9111b9eb1d7835ea7bea5b425dced73)
---
 include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h b/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h
index 618f0ee..d637daa 100644
--- a/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h
+++ b/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h
@@ -32,6 +32,10 @@
 #pragma warning(push)
 #pragma warning(disable:4067)    /* newline for __has_include_next */
 
+#ifndef __has_include_next
+#define __has_include_next(x) 0
+#endif
+
 #if defined(__clang__) && __has_include_next(<stdatomic.h>)
    /* use the clang stdatomic.h with clang-cl*/
 #  include_next <stdatomic.h>
-- 
2.56.0.windows.4

